{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"001e2b91-640f-4174-9d64-d8b33f6212f3","runId":"775851c4-0c0d-4252-b5f0-2186c0f8562e","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":12,"previousEventHash":"sha256:2f4d8c73f24b821d36bffbabeb5a1572366ead7709b43c3ff1a80de52db3ca1c","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04357-40e0-7ab3-a667-f1d39d899532","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:12:29.584Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:68a56515-b719-40cf-b43f-8f9b801f08a9","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:68a56515-b719-40cf-b43f-8f9b801f08a9","digest":"sha256:6a2dc9133011b0e510278f4b6ed67e4113e76ca3d95caaa1f6518c6565e7a53f"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"0648a313-d69d-4cd9-aac7-fdbb9e094fbd","runId":"775851c4-0c0d-4252-b5f0-2186c0f8562e","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:97b484cb5adcb2b7246659c46ad0fccf5fc567ab66c705596975eb350f38bf36","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04357-40e0-7ab3-a667-f1d39d899532","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:13:53.667Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verdict | Invalid |\n| Confidence | High |\n| Severity | High |\n| Task Type | Production-safety regression |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\nThe issue claims pnpm's `--filter-prod` selector is omitted from an option list, so `pnpm --filter-prod web test` can pass preflight against the root package and later execute a different workspace.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe frozen `staging` base has no package-selector allowlist. `packageScriptName` rejects every recognized package-manager command whose first post-executable argument begins with `-`. Therefore `pnpm --filter-prod web test` reaches `unsupportedPackageManagerOptionsError` and fails closed before execution. The reported bypass is not reproducible at the assigned base.\n\nFocused coverage currently exercises npm selectors, but it does not name pnpm's `--filter-prod`. Adding that regression case will preserve the existing fail-closed behavior explicitly.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe finding describes an earlier patch shape that is not present at frozen base `297621681ac15a325eed4d51903ada13c7330423`. The integrated implementation uses a broader option rejection rule, while the regression suite lacks an explicit pnpm `--filter-prod` case.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n| Path | Finding |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/adapters/verification-preflight.ts` | Existing `command.startsWith(\"-\")` guard already rejects `--filter-prod`. |\n| `test/adapters/verification-preflight.test.ts` | Selector regression matrix does not explicitly include pnpm `--filter-prod`. |\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `packageScriptName` recognizes `pnpm` and rejects a first command argument beginning with `-`.\n- `unsupportedPackageManagerOptionsError` fails closed with a tracked-verification configuration error.\n- Existing tests cover npm `--prefix`, `--workspace`, `--registry`, and delimiter misuse but not pnpm `--filter-prod`.\n\n### History Findings\n\nThe issue originates from review finding `correctness-argv-3` on PR #192 / issue #111. The frozen integration base contains a generalized package-manager option rejection implementation rather than the selector-list behavior described by that review finding.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nKeep production code unchanged and add a focused pnpm `--filter-prod` regression case to the existing malformed-root selector test. This is the narrowest change that validates current behavior and prevents the reported bypass from reappearing.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- #111 — source issue referenced by the review finding.\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The work is a single focused test-only regression.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the finding against the current integration branch.\n- [x] Confirm the root cause is already fixed by the generalized option rejection guard.\n- [ ] Add focused regression coverage for `pnpm --filter-prod`.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact remediation head with correctness and security reviewers.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
